    guide: [{ heading: "How FD maturity is calculated", body: "Indian term deposits compound quarterly under Reserve Bank convention through A = P multiplied by (1+r/400) raised to four times t. Principal P seeds computation, nominal rate r sets velocity, tenure t exponentiates compounding. Illustrate Rs 5,00,000 at 7% for five years maturing near Rs 7,07,390 with Rs 2,07,390 interest and 7.19% effective yield; senior 7.50% elevates same deposit near Rs 7,25,381 with Rs 2,25,381 interest. Tenure ladder matrix clarifies progression: one year Rs 5,35,216 | three years Rs 6,15,720 | five years Rs 7,07,390. Quarterly reinvestment outpaces annual payout elections because interim earnings immediately attract subsequent interest. Cumulative options maximize terminal corpus, whereas non-cumulative disbursements sacrifice compounding for cash flow. All arithmetic executes offline inside browser memory without transmitting account specifics. See /terms." }, { heading: "Inputs, rate choices and limitations", body: "Provide deposit quantum, card rate, tenure years, depositor category, and payout preference; engine returns maturity, interest aggregate, effective annualized yield, and quarterly accretion chart. General depositors incur 10% TDS once annual interest surpasses Rs 40,000, seniors face identical levy beyond Rs 50,000, with Form 15G or 15H shielding eligible nil-taxpayers. Premature liquidation typically forfeits 0.50-1.00% from contracted slab plus applicable TDS, transforming 7% five-year promise into 6% realized outcome. Senior augmentation of 0.50% meaningfully compounds: Rs 5,00,000 at 7.50% outpaces standard 7% by roughly Rs 18,000 across five years. Floating card revisions, penalty schedules, and tax brackets invalidate static projections. Scrutinize sanction advice for compounding periodicity, auto-renewal clauses, and nomination formalities. Juxtapose post-tax harvests against /ppf-calculator exemptions and /sip-calculator market prospects. See /terms." }, { heading: "Next steps and common questions", body: "Distribute Rs 5,00,000 across one-, three-, and five-year rungs rather than concentrating entire corpus in solitary maturity; maturing proceeds systematically reinvest at prevailing peaks while preserving emergency access. Compare standard Rs 7,07,390 against senior Rs 7,25,381 to motivate family-member allocations where eligible. Model premature scenario where year-three withdrawal at 6% penalty-adjusted rate yields near Rs 5,95,000 instead of anticipated trajectory, underscoring commitment discipline. Calendarize renewals, enable maturity alerts, and stagger institutions to diversify credit exposure beyond deposit insurance ceilings. Reconcile guaranteed but taxable FD harvests with EEE PPF compounding at /ppf-calculator and inflation-adjusted lenses at /inflation-calculator. This tutorial enlightens rather than advises asset allocation. Validate card rates, TDS certificates, and penalty grids with branch officials. See /methodology for algebra and /terms for disclaimers before booking." }]
